u are saying—that the field is heavily populated by introverts—the point about him being a "unicorn" is even more relevant. If he is an outgoing, highly social person entering a field dominated by introverts, he is going to stand out in the best way possible to recruiters and hiring managers. You can validate his fears by telling him, "You're right, studies actually show that a lot of math majors are highly introverted, so the vibe in your classes might be pretty quiet." But you can follow it up by reminding him that a college campus is huge. He doesn't have to fit the mold of his classmates to succeed in the major, and he has total control over who he hangs out with when class is over.
