borhood, and are overwhelmed. So, you are completely right: it is not random chance. You are observing a very real, very consistent pattern of incompetence. I just look at that pattern and blame the local management, the high turnover, and the broken GPS systems, rather than assuming the workers themselves are inherently unintelligent. But at the end of the day, whether it's a bad GPS, a terrible local manager, or a genuinely clueless driver, the result is the same for you: your packages are getting messed up, and you have every right to be fed up with it.
